The '''2026 South Tyneside Metropolitan Borough Council election''' were held on 7 May 2026, alongside the [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections across the United Kingdom]] being held on the same day. All 54 members of [[South Tyneside Metropolitan Borough Council]] will be elected.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Local government elections - Thursday 7 May 2026 |url=https://www.southtyneside.gov.uk/article/29169/Local-government-elections-Thursday-7-May-2026 |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=South Tyneside Council |language=en}}</ref> The election was held after boundary changes.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-01 |title=Everything you need to know about unprecedented South Tyneside local elections |url=https://www.shieldsgazette.com/news/politics/council/everything-you-need-to-know-about-unprecedented-south-tyneside-2026-local-elections-5459628 |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=Shields Gazette |language=en}}</ref>

Council leader Tracey Dixon was not re-elected in her Whitburn and Marsden ward as incumbent party [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] returned just one councillor.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.shieldsgazette.com/news/south-tyneside-council-leader-loses-her-seat-in-the-2026-local-election-8514405|title=South Tyneside Council leader loses her seat in the 2026 local election|date=8 May 2026|website=Shields Gazette|accessdate=9 May 2026}}</ref><ref name="auto">{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cpvprrwelxpo|title=Reform UK wins control of South Tyneside Council with 41 seats|date=8 May 2026|website=BBC News|accessdate=9 May 2026}}</ref> [[Reform UK]], who held no seats on the council prior to the election, won a majority of the councillors with 41, whilst 10 [[Green Party of England and Wales|Green Party]] councillors were elected alongside two independents.<ref name="auto"/>

== Background ==
In [[2024 South Tyneside Metropolitan Borough Council election|2024]], [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] retained control of the council.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Binding |first=Chris |date=2024-04-09 |title=Full list of South Tyneside Council local election 2024 candidates |url=https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/north-east-news/southtyneside-council-local-elections-2024-28965249 |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=Chronicle Live |language=en}}</ref>

